Fictional Meridian teaching case No course example grants workplace

00:00:05.468 --> 00:00:11.402
authority Requests and unverified claims are not approvals Which

00:00:11.468 --> 00:00:14.889
parts of the agreement depend on another owner’s confirmation

00:00:15.757 --> 00:00:19.271
Give two examples and explain why Daniel cannot confirm

00:00:19.376 --> 00:00:23.692
them for that owner Access decisions and spending 3

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:30.494
Diary access and protected information Daniel receives approved delegated

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.007
access sufficient to coordinate availability and business arrangements Private

00:00:36.073 --> 00:00:39.797
commitments may appear as unavailable periods without a personal

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:44.994
explanation Where a private commitment affects agreed protective coverage

00:00:45.428 --> 00:00:49.376
the necessary operational information goes through the approved restricted

00:00:49.468 --> 00:00:53.100
route The existence of a protected block is not

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:56.678
permission to investigate its purpose or disclose its detail

00:00:57.613 --> 00:01:02.744
4 Routine decision authority Daniel may arrange and move

00:01:02.784 --> 00:01:07.244
routine internal administrative meetings within agreed available periods when

00:01:07.336 --> 00:01:12.705
no protected commitment external undertaking cost or specialist dependency

00:01:12.718 --> 00:01:18.192
is affected Changes to executive decision meetings external visits

00:01:18.297 --> 00:01:23.402
or protected periods require the identified decision-maker's approval A

00:01:23.442 --> 00:01:26.468
request received directly by Lindiwe is entered into the

00:01:26.521 --> 00:01:30.389
controlled process before others are told that consequential arrangements

00:01:30.442 --> 00:01:36.165
are complete 5 Spending and supplier authority In this

00:01:36.165 --> 00:01:40.284
fictional example only Daniel may place orders for pre-approved

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:44.902
meeting consumables up to R2 000 per event within

00:01:44.915 --> 00:01:49.178
an already approved budget and supplier process He may

00:01:49.205 --> 00:01:52.836
not split purchases to avoid the limit He may

00:01:52.902 --> 00:01:56.376
prepare a quotation comparison for larger expenditure but may

00:01:56.428 --> 00:01:59.889
not approve it or release payment A change to

00:01:59.915 --> 00:02:03.284
supplier payment details goes to finance through the approved

00:02:03.363 --> 00:02:08.389
independent verification route The executive's preference for a supplier

00:02:08.442 --> 00:02:10.284
does not remove these conditions
